### 🗂️ 1. Command Center Sync
- [ ] Open GitHub Projects Kanban board.
- [ ] Review **This Week** (Ensure max 5 cards).
- [ ] Pull max 3 tasks into **Today**. 
  - *Note: If there are more than 3, move the excess back to This Week or Backlog.*

### ⏱️ 2. The 45-Minute Rhythm
*Rules: Set a 45-minute timer. Work strictly within these blocks. Stop immediately when the timer ends to preserve momentum.*

- [ ] **15 Min: Create Content**
  - [ ] Draft/finalize one LinkedIn post OR YouTube script.
- [ ] **15 Min: Build or Fix**
  - [ ] Work on exactly one task from your **Today** column for the site.
- [ ] **15 Min: Engage**
  - [ ] Reply to comments.
  - [ ] DM 3 people.

### ✅ 3. Shutdown & Celebrate
- [ ] Move completed cards to **Done**.

### 🧠 4. The Emotional Reframe
> **Read before closing out:**
> You are not behind. You are early.
> You don’t need a perfect business. You need a minimum lovable launch.
> Done is better than perfect.
> One product. One page. One payment link. One post per day.
> That’s how this gets built — not in a weekend, but in small, consistent steps.
